    "q-163240": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163240",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=y+{x}^{2}$ on the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le 2x\\}$ given that the area of the region is $2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{D}y+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{2x}y+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{x}^{2}y]_{y=x}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{3}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(8-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
